{"archetypes":[{"name":"bash-exit-propagation","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The new phase_tracking state machine uses || return 0 patterns combined with global variable mutations that are bash-specific and outside what generic correctness reviewers typically audit.","prompt_body":"Focus on whether `run_larch_log_init ... || return 0` correctly propagates bail state: when `run_larch_log_init` calls `tracking_init_failed` (mutating `IMPLEMENT_BAIL_REASON` and `STALL_TRACKING`) and returns 1, verify the `|| return 0` in both Branch 1 and Branch 2 callers correctly exits `phase_tracking` with the bail state already written to globals before the return fires. Verify that no state-mutating global assignments happen inside subshell command substitutions — all `BRANCH_SELECTED`, `ISSUE_NUMBER_RESOLVED`, `RUN_ID`, `DEFERRED`, and `STALL_TRACKING` mutations in `phase_tracking` must occur in the main shell, not inside `$(...)` expansions, which silently discard variable changes. Check whether `BRANCH_SELECTED` is always assigned to a non-empty value before every early `return 0` in `phase_tracking`, so `emit_final_tail`'s branch-aware `ISSUE_NUMBER` logic never operates on a stale empty `BRANCH_SELECTED` that falls into the wrong case arm. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"kv-wire-contract","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff adds five new KV keys to implement-bootstrap.sh's stdout protocol and extends the _ib_kv_scan whitespace-token parser in SKILL.md; any mismatch silently produces empty orchestrator variables without an error signal.","prompt_body":"Inspect `emit_final_tail` in `scripts/implement-bootstrap.sh` for completeness: verify that the branch-aware `ISSUE_NUMBER` logic covers every `IMPLEMENT_BAIL_REASON` value, particularly `tracking-init-failed` which should fall into the `*)` catch-all and emit `ISSUE_NUMBER_RESOLVED` when set (preserving the issue number for Step 18's stalled-rename path). Check `_ib_kv_scan` in `skills/implement/SKILL.md` to confirm the whitespace-token scanner correctly extracts all five new keys (`BRANCH_SELECTED`, `DEFERRED`, `STALL_TRACKING`, `ISSUE_NUMBER`, `RUN_ID`) when values contain hyphens like `branch-2-adopt` or are empty strings like `ISSUE_NUMBER=`. Verify the mandatory routing guard code block in SKILL.md correctly routes `DEFERRED=true` with empty `IMPLEMENT_BAIL_REASON` to continue (not skip) versus `STALL_TRACKING=true` to skip, and that `export ... BRANCH_SELECTED DEFERRED STALL_TRACKING IMPLEMENT_BAIL_REASON` is present so later Bash blocks can read these values. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"fork-carve-out-binding","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The fork mode carve-out replaces a hard-bail with best-effort upstream context fetch, a binding behavior change; downstream orchestration must consistently treat ISSUE_NUMBER as empty in fork mode to prevent spurious Closes #N injection.","prompt_body":"Verify that the `forked_target=true` path in `phase_tracking` leaves `ISSUE_NUMBER_RESOLVED` empty so `emit_final_tail`'s `forked-target-skip` case emits an empty `ISSUE_NUMBER`, and that the SKILL.md `_ib_kv_scan` block correctly exports an empty `ISSUE_NUMBER` rather than falling back to `TARGET_ISSUE_NUMBER` from the orchestrator scope. Check that `get-issue-context.sh` is invoked only when both `UPSTREAM_REPO_OPT` and `ISSUE_NUMBER_OPT` are non-empty per the guard at `scripts/implement-bootstrap.sh`, and that a failure of that call (guarded with `|| true`) cannot overwrite or corrupt any phase_tracking globals through an unexpected non-zero exit that propagates. Confirm that the SKILL.md bootstrap invocation block's `_ib_fork=()` array correctly gates `--upstream-repo "$UPSTREAM_REPO"` so that `--upstream-repo` is never passed without `--forked-target true`, avoiding the `die_usage` path that requires `--issue-number` with `--upstream-repo`. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
